    "raw_public_english_response": "Submission complete. Summary of the Registry V2 stress experiment outcome:\n\n**Planned settings (ORCA, opt accessor / freq task):**\n- Functional: **B3LYP** — `exact_registered`, loader accepted, renderer preserved.\n- Basis: **def2-TZVP** — canonical literal matched (`def2-TZVP` → `def2tzvp`), loader accepted, renderer preserved, but registry status is **`blocked_validation_coverage`** (`scientific_settings.v2.validation_coverage_gap`; project-candidate ineligible; evidence ceiling `loader_renderer_verification_only`; deterministic validator not enforced).\n\n**Fe ECP question — answer:** The pinned BSE definition (bse-catalog-0.11, via entry `setting.orca.method_basis.a6d92a427e69b3a7c59a`) is registered, but this arm exposes **no element-level ECP/coverage receipt for Fe (or Cl)**. Whether the BSE def2-TZVP embeds an Fe ECP therefore **cannot be confirmed from available evidence**, so `scientific_settings.basis.ecp_applicability_required` and `scientific_settings.basis.request_element_coverage_required` remain undischarged. Element findings for Cl and Fe record `covered=false, orbital_present=false, ecp_present=false, ecp_electrons=null` to reflect absent evidence — not confirmed absence.\n\n**Final proposal (as normalized):**\n- readiness: `blocked_validation_coverage`\n- blocking_rule_ids: `scientific_settings.basis.ecp_applicability_required`, `scientific_settings.basis.request_element_coverage_required`, `scientific_settings.v2.validation_coverage_gap` (set-order canonicalized)\n- settings: B3LYP / def2-TZVP, heavy_elements `[Fe]`, `freq` filled to `true` by the case-bound normalizer\n- No project written, no native input, no command, no execution (receipt `e253696e85f931923ce0ed212cc43bacb62f3441e804a11b60fa08f2f4eff3d2`).\n\nThe proposal is blocked pending validation coverage that would actually verify the def2-TZVP definition for Cl/Fe (including the Fe ECP question) — none of the blocked statuses were rewritten.",
